{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO coverage: units first built on or before October 1, 1978","requirement":"The City's Rent Stabilization Ordinance applies to rental properties first built on or before October 1, 1978, including apartments, condominiums, townhomes, duplexes, ADUs, JADUs, mobilehomes and hotel rooms rented for more than 30 days.","key_value":"built on or before 1978-10-01","coverage_conditions":"Rental properties first built on or before October 1, 1978 in the City of Los Angeles, plus replacement units under LAMC Section 151.28; includes apartments, condominiums, townhomes, duplexes, ADUs, JADUs, mobilehomes and hotel rooms occupied over 30 days.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Includes replacement units under LAMC Section 151.28"},"exemptions":"Rent amount is not regulated for condominium or townhome tenancies that commenced after December 31, 1995.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code ch. XV, art. 1 (Rent Stabilization Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Generally, the RSO applies to rental properties that were first built on or before October 1, 1978, as well as replacement units under
LAMC Section 151.28","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO annual rent increase limit","requirement":"For RSO units, a landlord may raise the rent only once in any 12-month period and only by the allowable rent increase percentage published by LAHD.","key_value":"once per 12 months; allowable annual percentage set by LAHD","coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code ch. XV, art. 1 (Rent Stabilization Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Rent may be increased once every 12 months by the allowable rent increase percentage","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO rent may rise to market rate after tenant vacates, is evicted or takes a buyout","requirement":"For RSO units, rent may be increased to the market rate when the tenant voluntarily moves out, is evicted for nonpayment or lease violation, is evicted under a Tenant Habitability Plan or City Attorney order, or accepts a Tenant Buyout Agreement.","key_value":"market rate","coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code ch. XV, art. 1 (Rent Stabilization Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Rent may be increased to the market rate if the tenant:
voluntarily moves out;
does not pay rent and is evicted;
violated the lease agreement and is evicted;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO utility add-on rent increase eliminated","requirement":"Beginning February 2, 2026, a landlord of an RSO unit may no longer include the additional percentage increase for utilities in the annual rent increase.","key_value":"no utility add-on increase","coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-02-02","citation":"L.A. Mun. Code ch. XV, art. 1 (Rent Stabilization Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Effective February 2, 2026, the landlord can no longer include an additional percentage increase for utilities.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO 10% additional-dependent rent increase eliminated","requirement":"Beginning February 2, 2026, the extra 10% rent increase for adding a dependent is no longer permitted; a 10% increase for an additional tenant is still allowed and may be charged within 60 days of the landlord learning of that tenant.","key_value":"no 10% dependent increase; 10% additional-tenant increase still allowed","coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-02-02","citation":"L.A. Mun. Code ch. XV, art. 1 (Rent Stabilization Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Effective February 2, 2026, an additonal 10% increase for an additional dependent added to the tenancy is no longer permitted. However, a 10% for an additional tenant is allowed (not a dependent) if moves into a rental unit","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO legal reasons for eviction (at-fault and no-fault)","requirement":"An RSO tenancy may be terminated only for stated at-fault causes (nonpayment, lease violation, nuisance, illegal use, refusal to renew, access denial, unapproved subtenant) or stated no-fault causes (owner move-in, resident manager, demolition, government order, conversion to affordable housing).","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 151.09","quoted_span":"Legal Reasons for Eviction
Tenant is at-fault
Failure to pay rent
Failure to fix or address a violation of the rental agreement","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO eviction notices must be filed with LAHD within three business days","requirement":"For RSO units, every notice terminating a tenancy must be filed with the Los Angeles Housing Department within three business days after it is served on the tenant.","key_value":"3 business days","coverage_conditions":"All rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code §§ 151.09, 165.05","quoted_span":"must be filed with the Los Angeles Housing Department (LAHD) within
three (3) business days of service on the tenant
per Los Angeles Municipal Code 151.09.C.9 & 165.05.B.5.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Relocation assistance required for RSO no-fault evictions","requirement":"A landlord who evicts an RSO tenant for a no-fault reason must pay tenant relocation assistance, file a Landlord Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD, and give 30-day and 60-day written notice (120 days or longer in some cases).","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance that are terminated for a no-fault reason.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code ch. XV, art. 1 (Rent Stabilization Ordinance)","quoted_span":"No-fault evictions require the payment of
relocation assistance.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Just Cause Ordinance covers rentals outside the RSO","requirement":"Rental properties in the City of Los Angeles that are not covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance are subject to the City's Just Cause Ordinance, which governs the rights of landlords and tenants on ending a tenancy.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental properties in the City of Los Angeles that are not covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Properties not covered by the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"City of Los Angeles Just Cause Ordinance","quoted_span":"Even if your property is not covered under the Rent Stabilization Ordinance, you and your tenants have rights and responsibilities under the
Just Cause Ordinance.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO covers interest payments on security deposits","requirement":"The Rent Stabilization Ordinance covers interest payments on security deposits, requiring landlords of RSO units to make interest payments on tenants' deposits.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code ch. XV, art. 1 (Rent Stabilization Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Interest Payments on Security Deposits","interaction":null,"confidence":0.5,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
